---
/**
 * QA / 検証記録 — PR #19, and the reason it is not a third decision case.
 *
 * #31 HD-J decided what this record IS: the log of the QA run made before
 * publication, kept as a range that was checked and a range that was not.
 * `HowIBuildCases.astro` said so in a comment and then drew it as a third `.dc`
 * under 判断事例's own head, after two cases, separated from them by the same
 * hairline that separates case one from case two. A reader counting blocks
 * counted three cases, because three blocks is what the page showed.
 *
 * #52 makes the structure agree with the decision. This is a section of its
 * own with its own `<h2>`, outside `#decision-cases` — so the two cases are
 * two, and this is a record beside them rather than the last of them.
 *
 * SHAPED SO IT CANNOT BECOME ONE. There is no 問題 and no 判断 here, because
 * the record has neither: what it has is what was covered, what was not, and
 * what was left unfixed on purpose. The fields a case has are the fields that
 * would invite writing the two this record does not hold.
 *
 * NO NEW SENTENCE WAS WRITTEN FOR THIS SECTION. `qa.summary` already says what
 * the record is — 「公開前に行った最終 QA の記録。直した件数ではなく、どこまで
 * 確認したか…」 — so a lead above it would be the same sentence twice, in the
 * site's voice the second time. The head names it; the summary explains it;
 * the facts are the record; the PR is where it can be checked.
 */
import { publicPrUrl } from '../../lib/content/derive.ts';
import { site } from '../../lib/content/site.ts';
import { ui } from '../../lib/content/ui.ts';

const qa = site.howIBuild.qaRecord;

/** Same reason as the cases section's: two places, one literal. */
const HEADING_ID = 'qa-record-head';
---

{/*
  DRAWN WITH WHAT THE PAGE ALREADY HAS. A mono label on the 2px rule — the
  section head 判断事例 and ROLES both use — the same `.dc` record, the same
  hairline list, the same `.lk` out to the PR. No box, no card, no second
  accent colour: what separates this from the section above it is the rule and
  the section rhythm, which is what separates every other pair of sections on
  this site.

  No rail label. `.tr > .fld` is placed in the second track explicitly, so the
  instrument column is simply empty here — and the one word that could go in it
  is the word already standing as the heading, which is the double announcement
  #31 removed from this page.
*/}
<section class="s-open" id="qa-record" aria-labelledby={HEADING_ID}>
  <div class="page">
    <div class="tr">
      <div class="fld">
        <div class="shead">
          <h2 class="mo" id={HEADING_ID}><b>{ui.howIBuild.qaLabel}</b></h2>
        </div>
        <div class="dc dc-qa" data-qa-record data-pr={qa.prNumber}>
          <h3 class="dc-t">{qa.title}</h3>
          <p class="dc-c">{qa.summary}</p>
          <ul class="dc-f">{qa.facts.map((f) => <li>{f}</li>)}</ul>
          <p class="dc-l m0">
            <a class="lk" href={publicPrUrl(qa.prNumber)} data-decision-pr={qa.prNumber}>
              {ui.howIBuild.openPr}<span class="ar">→</span>
            </a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
